WEBVTT

00:30:58.980 --> 00:31:01.057
AG: But that's more objective,

00:31:01.081 --> 00:31:03.613
"Let's try to get you to move
and communicate

00:31:03.637 --> 00:31:04.975
more like a normal person."

00:31:04.999 --> 00:31:07.875
AM: No one's ever told you
how to be more professor-ish.

00:31:08.810 --> 00:31:09.961
AG: No!

00:31:09.985 --> 00:31:14.030
AM: I think what sometimes
gets lost in this conversation

00:31:14.054 --> 00:31:16.178
when you talk to people
who work at companies

00:31:16.202 --> 00:31:18.987
that are telling them
to bring their whole selves to work,

00:31:19.011 --> 00:31:22.738
they often feel that the company
hasn't done the work necessary

00:31:22.762 --> 00:31:25.013
to receive them as they are.

00:31:25.037 --> 00:31:26.858
And it even seemed to me

00:31:26.882 --> 00:31:30.826
that the louder and the more insistent
an organization was